  "text": "Maqam Nairuz Maqam Yakah A member of the Maqam Rast Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of Nairuz Pronunciation of Yakah Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Nairuz starts with the root Jins Rast on the tonic , followed by Jins Bayati on the 5 th degree. Maqam Nairuz is quite rare by itself, but it is prominent as a sayr within Maqam Suznak / Maqam Rast – because of the affinity between Jins Bayati and Jins Hijaz on the 5 th scale degree. Maqam Yakah is an archaic version of Maqam Nairuz, based on note G3 in the Arabic archaic 24-tone scale (named “Yakah”) rather than note C4. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Rast Family . Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Nairuz by Sami Abu Shumays. Muwashah Ya Hilalan Firqat al-Musiqa al-Arabiyya (Egypt) Muwashah Mubarqa'u al-Jamal Hasan al-Haffar Music by ‘Umar al-Batsh Dawr Asl il-Gharam (1945) Nour el-Hoda Music by Muhammad ‘Uthman Ghannili Shwayy Shwayy (1945) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt)",
